{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/581522-beast-wait-aggravated-damage-ignores-armor","id":581522,"title":"[Beast] Wait, Aggravated damage ignores Armor?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-06T14:20:55-07:00","id":581522,"title":"[Beast] Wait, Aggravated damage ignores Armor?","content":"I mean, I know it ignores <i>Durability</i>, but this is the first I'm hearing about it ignoring Armor.<br /> <br /> If you don't know what I'm talking about, read the Satiety Expenditure effect of Unbreakable (page 172 of the preview.)<br /> <br /> Have I been missing something? This wasn't in Werewolf or in GMC.<br /> <br /> So ???","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T14:40:09-07:00","id":581552,"title":"","content":"I'm also not seeing this in previous books. That is curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T14:44:50-07:00","id":581558,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, probably not intended...hopefully will be addressed in the next draft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T14:54:55-07:00","id":581562,"title":"","content":"In 1e Aggravated had the potential to ignore mundane armor, though I'm not sure whether or not that's something that remains true in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T15:01:32-07:00","id":581566,"title":"","content":"Like Ashenrogue says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>World of Darkness Rulebook p.166</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attacks of a magical nature that inflict aggravated damage might not be hindered by armor; it depends on the type of attack. A sorcerous bolt of energy might pass right through armor. Mundane objects are simply not designed to withstand pure mystical assault. A silver letter opener stabbed at a werewolf, however, must still overcome armor to affect the creature (assuming it wears any armor). The werewolf's legendary Achilles' heel against silver doesn't give a letter opener a supernatural ability to ignore armor, only the power to blight a werewolf's flesh (if it can reach it). The Storyteller decides if an attack that inflicts aggravated damage also ignores armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>EDIT: I hope it stays that way, as attacks that rend objects like tissue paper should ignore mundane armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T15:10:04-07:00","id":581570,"title":"","content":"Looking through the books, Aggravated attacks do not ignore armour in general. Just potentially, and only if the damage is the result of a supernatural attack of a kind that makes sense to go through armour.<br /> Would be kind of weird if they did, silver daggers suddenly going through solid steel plates as if they were butter if worn by a Werewolf.<br /> <br /> the Satiety Expenditure effect of Unbreakable is probably meant to protect the Beast from supernatural effects that would make sense to go through armour, like the example &quot;A sorcerous bolt of energy might pass right through armor&quot; from the corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 07-06-2015, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T15:10:33-07:00","id":581572,"title":"","content":"It isn't &quot;attacks that rend objects like tissue paper&quot;, it's CERTAIN attacks of a magical nature that may ignore armor. Savage Rending, Protean Claws and Silver Jaws in the case of werewolves would all deal agg and still would have to exceed the armor reduction to inflict damage (armor that should be useless once its Durability has been reduced by blocking these atacks.) 1st ed Protean claws and Silver Jaws are most certainly magical in nature but wouldn't ignore armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 07-06-2015, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T18:48:38-07:00","id":581797,"title":"","content":"Isn't that what the &quot;Piercing&quot; attribute should be specifically for, though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T19:18:40-07:00","id":581823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/581522-beast-wait-aggravated-damage-ignores-armor?p=581797#post581797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that what the &quot;Piercing&quot; attribute should be specifically for, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, piercing is for things that are part of a broader category that would normally be stopped by armor (such as bullets), but are specially designed to bypass a portion of that armor (e.g. armor piercing bullets). A giant ball of fire (magical or non), bolt of lightning (likewise, magical or non), or a direct assault on the mystical energy holding a person together (probably not non-magical) doesn't &quot;pierce&quot; or &quot;penetrate&quot; armor in the sense that it is more capable of punching through it, it bypasses it because the armor is not designed to protect against such an assault at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T19:24:47-07:00","id":581827,"title":"","content":"Then I suppose it should be more sensible to directly put it under the 'armour coverage' rules then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T03:20:01-07:00","id":582073,"title":"","content":"I read the satiety effect as:<br /> Bashing is negated<br /> Lethal is downgraded<br /> Aggravated remains aggravated<br /> Armor from the normal and low effects only affects aggravated attacks<br /> <br /> It would be a vague way to indicate that the armor's affects are superseded by downgrading damage or damage negation. Adding 'only' to the sentence would make it clear. Also, I think the 4/3 is wrong. Can't you have satiety and normal? Normal and low effects have different armor ratings. Normal is 3/2.<br /> <br /> Attacks that bypass or pierce armor would work on the armor if applicable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T03:34:28-07:00","id":582096,"title":"","content":"Satiety expenditure is explicitly cumulative with the other effects. If you get armour vs bashing without it, you get it with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T12:42:25-07:00","id":582634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/581522-beast-wait-aggravated-damage-ignores-armor?p=581572#post581572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't &quot;attacks that rend objects like tissue paper&quot;, it's CERTAIN attacks of a magical nature that may ignore armor. Savage Rending, Protean Claws and Silver Jaws in the case of werewolves would all deal agg and still would have to exceed the armor reduction to inflict damage (armor that should be useless once its Durability has been reduced by blocking these atacks.) 1st ed Protean claws and Silver Jaws are most certainly magical in nature but wouldn't ignore armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking a bit more about it I agree. I would probably let 1st ed Savage Rending and Protean Claws also damage the Armor, and let the reduction by Armor stop applying only after the armor is shredded enough. Silver Jaws would not degrade armor, as silver only inflicts Aggravated damage to werewolves, and not to objects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T18:31:09-07:00","id":582948,"title":"","content":"I remember Cold Iron could bypass magical defenses of Gentry or Changeling. But no, the only method I know that can bypass mundane armor is armor piercing. So a Mortal with 2/0 armor gets stabbed by another mortal with a knife that had armor piercing 1, it would bypass 1 armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6740-goblin-engineer","name":"Goblin Engineer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T19:22:17-07:00","id":583062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/581522-beast-wait-aggravated-damage-ignores-armor?p=582096#post582096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satiety expenditure is explicitly cumulative with the other effects. If you get armour vs bashing without it, you get it with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Armor vs. damage that will be negated is irrelevant. I'm not sure about downgraded damage &quot;trumping&quot; armor. I'm not familiar with that occurring before. My take is Satiety has no affect on aggravated damage. As you say, it is cumulative with one of the others and the last sentence of satiety doesn't seem to add anything except confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}